cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use swiftrel, please cite it as below, and also cite vcftools, whose behaviour it reproduces."
title: "swiftrel: a byte-identical drop-in replacement for vcftools --relatedness2"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-04
license: LGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/joe-b-christensen/swiftrel"
authors:
  - family-names: Christensen
    given-names: Joe
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-0908-1299"
    email: joechristensen@clin.au.dk
    affiliation: "Translational Neuropsychiatry Unit (TNU), Department of Clinical Medicine, Aarhus University, Denmark"
keywords:
  - relatedness
  - kinship
  - KING
  - vcftools
  - performance
abstract: >-
  swiftrel computes the KING-robust kinship statistics of vcftools --relatedness2 with output byte-identical to
  vcftools 0.1.17 for every supported option and thread count. On four real 1000 Genomes sets it was 470x faster
  than vcftools, and on seven sets 6.0x faster than PLINK 2 --make-king-table run from the same VCF, which computes
  a different estimator (geometric means, two threads, AVX-512 CPU).
